<span id="workspaces-title" class="anchor-alias" aria-hidden="true"></span><span
  id="workspaces-close-title"
  class="anchor-alias"
  aria-hidden="true"></span>
<section
  class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top"
  aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-0"
>
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">your sets of tabs</p><h2
      id="workspaces-section-0"
    >
      Name it once. Keep it up to date as you browse.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Save this window or start a new set</h3><p>
        Open the workspace control in the command panel or type /workspace.
        Active Patrons can save the current window or create a blank named
        workspace.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Return without rebuilding the set</h3><p>
        A bound workspace automatically saves its tabs and groups as you browse
        and returns after relaunch. Switching replaces the current window’s set;
        a workspace already open elsewhere brings that window forward.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>You decide what belongs together</h3><p>
        Create groups and assign tabs yourself. Blanc saves those choices; it
        does not detect tasks or organize tabs by meaning.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="workspaces-section-1">
  <div>
    <p class="section-kicker">part of Patron</p><h2 id="workspaces-section-1">
      Support Blanc and keep your saved workspaces.
    </h2>
  </div>
  <div class="feature-copy-list">
    <article>
      <h3>Available on every desktop platform</h3><p>
        Browsing essentials and ordinary tab groups are free. Blanc Patron is
        the optional subscription: US$30 per year or US$4 per month, plus
        applicable tax. It adds saved Named Workspaces. Creating a named
        workspace requires an active Patron subscription. Named Workspaces are
        available on macOS, Windows and Linux.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Existing workspaces remain yours</h3><p>
        If membership lapses, existing workspaces remain openable, switchable,
        and automatically updated. Renaming and removing existing workspaces
        continue to work if it lapses. Earlier one-time supporters keep their
        lifetime Patron access.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h3>Keep private browsing separate</h3><p>
        Private tabs are excluded from saved workspaces. When a switch would
        discard private tabs or an unsaved window, Blanc asks you to make an
        explicit choice.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
<aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="workspaces-note-title">
  <p class="section-kicker">good to know</p><h2 id="workspaces-note-title">
    Saved on this device, within this profile.
  </h2>
  <p>
    Named Workspaces are device-local and profile-scoped. They do not sync
    across devices or move tabs between local profiles. Saving a workspace
    preserves its tab setup, not every page’s running state.
  </p>
  <a
    class="text-link"
    href="/#home-patron-title"
    data-track="feature_cta_click"
    data-feature="named-workspaces"
    data-cta-position="related-feature"
    >Explore Blanc Patron <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
  >
</aside>
